{{also|Boxen}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|boxen|lang=enm}}, replacing earlier {{term|bixen|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|byxen||made of boxwood|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|box|en}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# Made of [[boxwood]].
# Resembling [[box]] (the wood).

===Etymology 2===
{{suffix|box|en|pos2=plural marker}}

A nonstandard plural of {{term|box}} formed by analogy with {{term|oxen}}. The standard plural of ''box'' is {{term|boxes}}; ''-en'' is no longer a plural in standard use. See ''[[-en#Etymology 2|-en]]'' for details.

====Noun====
{{infl|en|noun|plural}}

# {{context|computing|slang}} Multiple [[computer]]s (or occasionally a single computer), especially those running [[Unix|UNIX]].
#* '''1996,''' Siu Ha Vivian Chu, ''[http://groups.google.com/group/comp.os.linux.networking/browse_thread/thread/df52b9232607769c/9eeba5e6056bb696?lnk=st&q=&rnum=1#9eeba5e6056bb696   DEC vt320 → linux boxen]'' in comp.os.linux.networking
#*: i can't seem to find any how-to regarding connecting a terminal to a linux '''boxen''' via parallel port...
#* '''2002,''' Gregory Seidman, ''[http://groups.google.com/group/muc.lists.debian.user/browse_thread/thread/f622a3da1225f845/7aecf55aabe92b83?lnk=st&q=boxen&rnum=4#7aecf55aabe92b83  serving debian to redhat boxen]'' in muc.lists.debian.user
#*: Furthermore, it is necessary that all four Linux '''boxen''' have the same development environment...

